     <h2>3. Recording of data on our website</h2>
     <p><strong>Cookies</strong></p>
     <p>In some instances, our website and its pages use so-called cookies. Cookies do not cause any damage to your computer and do not contain viruses. The purpose of cookies is to make our website more user friendly, effective and more secure. Cookies are small text files that are placed on your computer and stored by your browser.</p>
+
+    <p>We use a single session cookie, set only when you save an article to your reading list. It stores the article identifiers you saved and nothing else; it is strictly necessary for that feature.</p>
+
+    <h2>4. Data minimization</h2>
+    <p>We collect only what is needed to provide the service. Reading is possible without an account. For sign-in and registration we process only a username and password, which are sent directly to our authentication service and are never stored in your browser or shared with analytics.</p>
+
+    <h2>5. Third-party services</h2>
+    <ul>
+        <li><strong>Google Fonts</strong> (fonts.googleapis.com, fonts.gstatic.com): delivers the headline typeface; your IP address is transmitted to Google when fonts load.</li>
+        <li><strong>Analytics</strong> (us-central1-web-devrel-apps.cloudfunctions.net): loaded only if you click “Accept analytics”. It is never loaded if your browser sends Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control signals. You can change your choice at any time via “Manage Privacy Preferences” in the footer.</li>
+        <li><strong>Authentication service</strong> (same host as above): receives your credentials when you sign in or register.</li>
+    </ul>
+    <p>Third-party integrations are reviewed and documented in <code>docs/THIRD_PARTY_AUDIT.md</code> whenever one is added or changed.</p>
+
+    <h2>6. Security</h2>
+    <p>This site is served with a strict Content Security Policy, HSTS, and related security headers. API responses are not cached.</p>
 </LegalLayout>
